IMPORT `ito-il08-tax-years`
IMPORT `ito-s1-israeli-resident`
IMPORT `ito-s2-sources-of-income`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Tests for s 1 ("Israeli resident" (a)) and s 2. Row IL-08.
-- Expected values from the text at lines 143-163 and 209-245; none edited to match the code.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Tests — sections 1 and 2`

§§ `Section 1 — "Israeli resident"`

GIVEN `the year`      IS A NUMBER
      `days`          IS A NUMBER
      `three years`   IS A NUMBER
      `finding`       IS A MAYBE `Where the centre of life is`
      `rebutted`      IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `An individual's year, for the definition of Israeli resident`
`in` `the year` `, days in Israel` `days` `, in three years` `three years` `, the finding` `finding` `, rebutted:` `rebutted` MEANS
    `An individual's year, for the definition of Israeli resident` WITH
        `tax year`                                                           IS `the year`
        `days in Israel in the tax year`                                     IS `days`
        `days in Israel in the tax year and the two tax years before it`     IS `three years`
        `the centre of life, as found on the whole of the individual's ties` IS `finding`
        `the presumption has been rebutted`                                  IS `rebutted`
        `regulations made under paragraph (4) reach the individual`          IS FALSE
        `section 14(b) reaches the individual in the tax year`               IS FALSE

-- (2)(a): 183 days or more. No finding, no rebuttal: presumed resident.
#ASSERT `s 1 "Israeli resident" (a) — an Israeli resident in the tax year:` (`in` 2026 `, days in Israel` 183 `, in three years` 183 `, the finding` NOTHING `, rebutted:` FALSE)
-- 182 days and 400 over three years: no presumption, and no finding: declined, not "not resident".
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 1 "Israeli resident" (a) — an Israeli resident in the tax year:` (`in` 2026 `, days in Israel` 182 `, in three years` 400 `, the finding` NOTHING `, rebutted:` FALSE) BECAUSE "no finding of the centre of life has been made, and no unrebutted presumption decides it"
-- (2)(b): 30 days and 425 over three years.
#ASSERT `s 1 "Israeli resident" (a)(2) — a presumption that the centre of life is in Israel arises, for` (`in` 2026 `, days in Israel` 30 `, in three years` 425 `, the finding` NOTHING `, rebutted:` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 1 "Israeli resident" (a) — an Israeli resident in the tax year:` (`in` 2026 `, days in Israel` 30 `, in three years` 425 `, the finding` NOTHING `, rebutted:` FALSE)
-- 29 days, however many over three years: (b) fails, (a) fails.
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 "Israeli resident" (a)(2) — a presumption that the centre of life is in Israel arises, for` (`in` 2026 `, days in Israel` 29 `, in three years` 900 `, the finding` NOTHING `, rebutted:` FALSE)
-- 30 days and 424 over three years: (b) fails.
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 "Israeli resident" (a)(2) — a presumption that the centre of life is in Israel arises, for` (`in` 2026 `, days in Israel` 30 `, in three years` 424 `, the finding` NOTHING `, rebutted:` FALSE)
-- (3): the presumption rebutted, and no finding recorded: declined.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 1 "Israeli resident" (a) — an Israeli resident in the tax year:` (`in` 2026 `, days in Israel` 200 `, in three years` 500 `, the finding` NOTHING `, rebutted:` TRUE) BECAUSE "no finding of the centre of life has been made, and no unrebutted presumption decides it"
-- (1): a finding governs, whatever the days: abroad with 200 days, in Israel with 10.
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 "Israeli resident" (a) — an Israeli resident in the tax year:` (`in` 2026 `, days in Israel` 200 `, in three years` 500 `, the finding` (JUST `outside Israel`) `, rebutted:` TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 1 "Israeli resident" (a) — an Israeli resident in the tax year:` (`in` 2026 `, days in Israel` 10 `, in three years` 50 `, the finding` (JUST `in Israel`) `, rebutted:` FALSE)
-- A tax year before 2024.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 1 "Israeli resident" (a) — an Israeli resident in the tax year:` (`in` 2023 `, days in Israel` 365 `, in three years` 1095 `, the finding` NOTHING `, rebutted:` FALSE) BECAUSE "row IL-08 does not hold the text of these sections for a tax year before 2024"
-- (4) and s 14(b), reached and not encoded.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 1 "Israeli resident" (a) — an Israeli resident in the tax year:` (`An individual's year, for the definition of Israeli resident` WITH `tax year` IS 2026, `days in Israel in the tax year` IS 365, `days in Israel in the tax year and the two tax years before it` IS 1095, `the centre of life, as found on the whole of the individual's ties` IS NOTHING, `the presumption has been rebutted` IS FALSE, `regulations made under paragraph (4) reach the individual` IS TRUE, `section 14(b) reaches the individual in the tax year` IS FALSE) BECAUSE "the regulations under paragraph (4) of the definition of Israeli resident are not encoded in this model"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 1 "Israeli resident" (a) — an Israeli resident in the tax year:` (`An individual's year, for the definition of Israeli resident` WITH `tax year` IS 2026, `days in Israel in the tax year` IS 365, `days in Israel in the tax year and the two tax years before it` IS 1095, `the centre of life, as found on the whole of the individual's ties` IS NOTHING, `the presumption has been rebutted` IS FALSE, `regulations made under paragraph (4) reach the individual` IS FALSE, `section 14(b) reaches the individual in the tax year` IS TRUE) BECAUSE "section 14(b) displaces the definition of Israeli resident, and is not encoded in this model"

§§ `Section 2 — the charge, and work income`

`a salary paid abroad`       MEANS `An item of income, for section 2` WITH `source` IS `employment`, `produced or accrued in Israel` IS FALSE, `amount` IS 50
`a salary paid in Israel`    MEANS `An item of income, for section 2` WITH `source` IS `employment`, `produced or accrued in Israel` IS TRUE, `amount` IS 100
`a dividend from abroad`     MEANS `An item of income, for section 2` WITH `source` IS `dividend, interest, linkage differences or discount`, `produced or accrued in Israel` IS FALSE, `amount` IS 7

-- A resident is charged on income produced or accrued anywhere; a foreign resident only in Israel.
#ASSERT `s 2 — the item is within the charge of section 2, for a person who is an Israeli resident:` TRUE `,` `a salary paid abroad`
#ASSERT NOT `s 2 — the item is within the charge of section 2, for a person who is an Israeli resident:` FALSE `,` `a salary paid abroad`
#ASSERT `s 2 — the item is within the charge of section 2, for a person who is an Israeli resident:` FALSE `,` `a salary paid in Israel`
#ASSERT `s 2 — the income within the charge of section 2, for a person who is an Israeli resident:` FALSE `, from` (LIST `a salary paid in Israel`, `a salary paid abroad`, `a dividend from abroad`) EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `s 2 — the income within the charge of section 2, for a person who is an Israeli resident:` TRUE `, from` (LIST `a salary paid in Israel`, `a salary paid abroad`, `a dividend from abroad`) EQUALS 157
-- s 1: work income is income under s 2(2).
#ASSERT `s 1 — work income:` `a salary paid abroad`
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 — work income:` `a dividend from abroad`
